       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ddfaabcc9635974ebed182e89941a947?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSB-2.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ddfaabcc9635974ebed182e89941a947?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSB-2.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Stephen Bayliss",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=6089a4cb543264006867626e",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>ParameterRequestWrapper is the culprit as this rewrites the output format to RDF/XML; with the filter subsequently picking up the correct format and then re-formatting it to the originally-requested format.</p>\n\n<p>The filter needs some work (ie handle different output formats correctly rather than rely on RDF/XML output).</p>\n\n<p>Fixed the parameter rewriting, but leaving this issue open as a placeholder to fix the RISearch filter itself.</p>",
     "created": "28/Apr/11 11:07 AM",
     "id": "11928",
     "jsdPublic": true,
     "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/10576/comment/11928",
